A||||0||mshill||V6 EGR Solenoid replacement...||||1||
Z||000000||mshill||08-10-2000||08:27 PM||||I have found a readily available replacement for the ever fragile, very expensive V6 Fiero EGR Solenoid.  I have taken one off of an 86-88 Pontiac 6000 that had a 2.8L engine.<P>These look slightly different than the Fiero solenoid.  They do not have a fitting for the fresh air hose on the end.  The filter housing is smaller in diameter, and it is mounted in the bracket facing the wrong direction.<P>I simply turned it around in the bracket, mounted it and plugged it into the vacuum lines.  I have 2000 miles on it without a code 32 and the engine runs the same as before and the old one used to give me intermittent code 32s.<P>I must have seen a hundred of these today while making my rounds at the sif service yards today.||||reg||1
